# GitHub Issues — agent reference

Product backlog on **`sprmke/kame-homes` GitHub Issues** — not duplicated in repo markdown.

## Source of truth

| Layer           | Location                                                                                   |
| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| Pending work    | https://github.com/sprmke/kame-homes/issues + Project board                                |
| Epic parents    | GitHub sub-issue parent (e.g. #104 for §4 emails) — see `docs/README.md` (Product backlog) |
| Shipped archive | `docs/archive/todos/shipped/`                                                              |

## Required skill

**`.cursor/skills/github-issues/SKILL.md`** or **`/github-issue`** when picking up, creating, or shipping issues. New teammates / QA: **`/kh-create-new-ticket`** (template) · **`/kh-help`**.

## Workflow

1. `bun scripts/dev/gh-issue.mjs view --github N`
2. Implement — update route guides / `PROJECT.md` when behavior changes
3. `bun scripts/dev/gh-issue.mjs ship --github N --notes "…"`

## Naming

- Epic: `[Epic N] …` (GitHub parent issue)
- Child: `[N.M] …` — use `--section N` on create; link with `--parent {epic#}`

## Don'ts

- Don't add Spec/Epic path footers to issue bodies
- Don't recreate local spec mirrors under `docs/todos/`
- Don't use `docs/planning/PENDING_BACKLOG.md` (retired)
- Don't attribute issues to Cursor
